      {
        "id": 105540,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-04T13:15:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trscroggs\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/b38774/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trscroggs:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Happy Thoughts wrote:</b><br><blockquote>1. Bjarlspire has a card called DrurSkjyld Converter which is a tech card that, each battle phase, says, \"Make the Ship Panel's [weaponry] equal to half of its Ship Panel's [defense], rounded down.\" The question here is, is that a virtual calculation that overrides the actual tokens, or do the physical tokens get adjusted to match the calculation from the card's text (presumably even if the actual installed weaponry is a higher value)? Sub-question: Is this a permanent modification to the ship's weaponry value, or one that just lasts for the current battle phase?\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nActually I have a few questions to this question as well. &nbsp;I think couple of scenarios will explain what I want to know better.\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>&nbsp;DrurSkjyld Converter is played and&nbsp;[defense]&nbsp;is 6, giving them an&nbsp;[weaponry]&nbsp;value of 3. &nbsp;Later thanks to some boosts the shields get to 8. &nbsp;Does the attack then go to 4? &nbsp;And if so, during what phase is that adjustment made?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>&nbsp;DrurSkjyld Converter is played and&nbsp;[defense]&nbsp;is 6, giving them an&nbsp;[weaponry]&nbsp;value of 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;During a unfortunate fight it loses 2 shields. &nbsp;Does the attack go down to 2? &nbsp;And if so is this evaluated before or after finishing the attack?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>&nbsp;DrurSkjyld Converter is played and&nbsp;[defense]&nbsp;is 6, giving them an&nbsp;[weaponry]&nbsp;value of 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;Later a boost gives&nbsp;Bjarlspire an additional attack token on the main card, giving a total of&nbsp; 4. &nbsp;Does the&nbsp;&nbsp;DrurSkjyld Converter then reduce this total back down to 3 because that is half the shields?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>&nbsp;DrurSkjyld Converter is played and&nbsp;[defense]&nbsp;is 6, giving them an&nbsp;[weaponry]&nbsp;value of 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;During a fight it gets a secondary boost increasing its defense to 8 for that fight only. &nbsp;Does the attack value get adjusted as well, and does it revert back at the end of the fight?</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Converter only converts shields from you Ship Panel, not your total defense value. Just clearing that up now. Generally though you are correct, if you had 8 shields on your ship panel, your weaponry on your panel would change to 4. But this conversion only happens during the Icon activation of the Battle Phase and works just like every other effect with a phase symbol in the game</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Converter only converts during the Icon activation of the Battle Phase. Damage Calculation has nothing to do with DrurSkjyld</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If you had 4 weaponry on your ship panel while activating Battle Icons and a defense of 6, yes your weaponry on your panel would be lowered to 3.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Again, this ability only activates during the Icon activation phase, just like every other Icon ability in the game. Converter is no exception.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Does that help any? Again, the card only deals with energy on your ship panel and <em>not</em> from any techs. And its an Icon activation, meaning it triggers once at the start of every battle phase with the other icons. After that, any change is permanent until the next time the ability triggers.</p>",
